Ambika (Mutable Instruments)
https://github.com/pichenettes/ambika
Copyright 2012 Emilie Gillet
Firmware under GPL-3.0-or-later; hardware and documentation under CC BY-SA 3.0.

The Ambika machine is a port of the voicecard firmware (voicecard/ and
common/: oscillators, mixer, envelopes, LFOs, modifiers, modulation
matrix), written in fy and following the firmware's arithmetic. It also
ships the firmware's lookup tables and its factory programs, which are not
ours to release under CC0 and stay under the firmware's license:
  kernels/06-voices/ambika.fy
  kernels/06-voices/ambika_tables.fy
  machines/ambika/ambika.fy
  machines/ambika/assets/tables.wav (the firmware's tables, packed)
  machines/ambika/presets/A, B, F, S (the golden card's programs, converted
    by tools/ambika/import_programs.py; the programs' authors are the
    card's; the card carries no license of its own, so it is treated as part
    of the firmware repository, GPL-3.0-or-later)
  tools/ambika/
The ten presets machines/ambika/presets/01-10 are ours, under CC0 1.0.
